From 1aa9026974edc8b70541c6fc87c3d47fb53fb581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:46:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(xtask): the quick submodule filter reads trait impls and
 scoped pub as shared

- quick_subs: impl Trait for Type, pub after attributes on one line, and
  pub(crate) / pub(super) / pub(in ..) count as shared: the whole suite runs.
- braces::code reads cr".." raw strings, and an escaped char literal ends
  at its last quote; a table test pins the lexer.
- scan::test_fns: the attribute walk stops at a line that holds a fn, and
  the loop always moves on (a test below `#[allow(..)] pub fn h() {}`
  looped forever); fn_re reads pub(..) and const/unsafe/extern fns.
- A fixture test runs a real `<sub>::` step: 1 passed, 4 filtered out.
- The loop variable `whole` is now `outside_fns`.

Fixes #3711

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
